# Neo Lo-Fi parameters (docs/specs/neo-lofi.md). The order changes only with a version (machines.md §3.2): songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoLoFi
namespace NeoBuzz.LoFi
class NeoLoFiMachine
summary Lo-fi in one effect, with zero latency: bit-depth reduction (1 to 24 bits, fractional, optional TPDF dither), sample-and-hold rate reduction down to 200 Hz with an optional anti-alias filter and hold-clock jitter, hiss (optionally following the input), vinyl crackle, light wow, flutter and drift, a tone control, Mix and Output. Everything is smoothed; with every stage off, or Mix at 0, the input passes bit for bit. Use it for 8-bit and early-sampler grit, cassette and radio colour, dusty vinyl, telephone and small-speaker sounds.

group Crush
Bits        "Bits"          0 2300 1100   lin 1 24 bit 1                  | Word length of the output in bits; 24 is off. Fractional values give a fractional number of levels
    how Sets the word length from 1 to 24 bits, in fractions of a bit; 24 turns the crusher off.
    sound Fewer bits give coarser steps: at 12 it is grainy on quiet parts, at 8 it is gritty, at 4 and below it is a harsh buzz of noise and distortion.
Dither      "Dither"        0 1     0     switch                          | TPDF dither (one step peak to peak each side) before the rounding
    how Adds triangular dither before the bit reduction.
    sound Off the quantisation error is crunchy distortion that follows the signal; on it turns into a smooth hiss, and quiet tails stay alive.
Rate        "Rate"          0 1000  1000  freq 200 192000                  | Sample-and-hold rate in Hz; at or above the host's sample rate it is off
    how Sets the rate the signal is held at, from 200 Hz up; the top of the range, at or above the song's sample rate, turns the reducer off.
    sound Lower rates sound crunchy and metallic as the top end folds back into the audible range; very low rates turn music into an electronic toy.
AntiAlias   "Anti-alias"    0 1     0     switch                          | A steep low-pass (8th order, 0.42 of the hold rate) before the hold
    how Filters everything above the new Nyquist frequency away before the hold.
    sound Off, the fold-over aliasing makes the sound harsh and inharmonic; on, the sound is duller but clean, like a period sampler's output filter.
Jitter      "Jitter"        0 1000  0     pct                             | Random timing error of the hold clock (up to 25% of a hold period at 100%)
    how Shakes the moment each sample is taken by a small random amount.
    sound A little roughens the aliasing into noise; more adds a rough, unstable grain.
group Noise
Hiss        "Hiss"          0 700   0     db -90 -20 inf                  | Hiss level in dBFS (RMS); off at its minimum
    how Adds a steady hiss from -90 to -20 dB, or turns it off at the minimum.
    sound A little hiss gives a worn tape or old preamp feel; more covers quiet passages.
HissFollow  "Hiss follow"   0 1     0     switch                          | The hiss follows the input's level, and closes when the input is silent (below -70 dBFS)
    how Makes the hiss follow the loudness of the input, gated off when nothing plays.
    sound The hiss rises and falls with the music, like noise that comes from the signal itself; silence stays silent.
Crackle     "Crackle"       0 1000  0     lin 0 100 /s 1                  | Vinyl dust: pops per second
    how Sets how many pops per second are added, from 0 to 100.
    sound A few pops a second sound like a dusty record; many sound like a worn one.
CrackleLevel "Crackle level" 0 540  300   db -60 -6                       | Peak level of the loudest pops in dBFS
    how Sets the level of the crackle pops, from -60 to -6 dB.
    sound Low levels are a faint dust under the music; high levels are loud clicks.
group Motion
Wow         "Wow"           0 500   0     lin 0 50 ct 1                   | Slow pitch variation: peak deviation in cents (the modulated read delays the sound by a few ms, never reported as latency)
    how Sets a slow pitch wobble of up to 50 cents.
    sound It gives a worn, unstable tape or turntable feel, with slow bending of long notes.
WowRate     "Wow rate"      0 1000  402   exp 0.3 6 Hz 2                  | The wow's rate
    how Sets the speed of the slow pitch wobble, from 0.3 to 6 Hz.
    sound Slow rates drift lazily and faster ones sound like a warble.
Flutter     "Flutter"       0 500   0     lin 0 50 ct 1                   | Fast pitch variation (7.3 and 11.9 Hz): peak deviation in cents
    how Sets a fast pitch wobble of up to 50 cents.
    sound It adds a fine, nervous shimmer to the pitch, like a tired transport.
Drift       "Drift"         0 250   0     lin 0 25 ct 1                   | Very slow random detune (three incommensurate slow waves, 0.12 to 0.31 Hz): peak deviation in cents
    how Sets a very slow, irregular detune of up to 25 cents.
    sound The pitch wanders slowly and never repeats exactly, like an unsteady oscillator or a warped record.
group Output
Tone        "Tone"          0 1000  500   bip                             | After the chain: left of centre a low-pass (20 kHz down to 600 Hz), right of centre a high-frequency lift (up to 9 dB)
    how Tilts the tone after everything else: darker to the left, brighter to the right, flat in the middle.
    sound Turn it down to soften the harsh edges of the crushing; turn it up to bring back air.
Mix         "Mix"           0 1000  1000  pct                             | Dry/wet (the dry signal is not delayed: there is no latency)
    how Blends the processed signal with the dry input.
    sound Lower values keep the original and add the lo-fi as a layer.
Output      "Output"        0 1000  500   db -24 24                       | Output level
    how Sets the final level in dB, from -24 to +24.
    sound It makes the sound louder or quieter without changing its character.
